<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Scattered movement reported.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Scattered movement reported.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain dealers in the High Plains said Tuesday they had seen scattered movement of hard red winter wheat over the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>&quot;We did buy some wheat yesterday. I'd say maybe over 100,000 bushels,&quot; said one dealer at an Oklahoma terminal elevator.</p>
<p>A dealer at a south Kansas terminal also reported buying over 100,000 bushels of HRW wheat as prices became more attractive to producers Monday.</p>
<p>But other Kansas merchandisers said movement of wheat was muted.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, more basis bids were rolled out to the March contract. Overall, bids were steady to slightly easier.</p>
